1
00:00:03,500 --> 00:00:08,055
Every week, a project manager spends hours collecting status from mail,

2
00:00:08,075 --> 00:00:12,593
meetings, chats and SharePoint, and still finds the risks too late.

3
00:00:12,893 --> 00:00:16,870
In the next few minutes, you will build a PM Agent in

4
00:00:16,890 --> 00:00:21,238
Microsoft 365 Copilot that does the collecting for you.

5
00:00:21,438 --> 00:00:27,121
A weekly status draft, early warnings on risks, and every finding traced to its source.

6
00:00:28,021 --> 00:00:29,088
Here is the idea.

7
00:00:29,108 --> 00:00:34,264
The agent reads the places where your project actually lives: your Outlook email,

8
00:00:34,284 --> 00:00:40,556
your Teams meetings and their transcripts, your Teams chats, and the project’s SharePoint site.

9
00:00:40,656 --> 00:00:44,278
From them, it prepares three things: the weekly status draft,

10
00:00:44,298 --> 00:00:48,378
risk alerts, and the decisions and actions you might have missed.

11
00:00:48,478 --> 00:00:49,700
You stay in charge.

12
00:00:49,720 --> 00:00:53,320
The agent prepares, and the project manager decides.

13
00:00:54,320 --> 00:00:56,524
Before you start, check four things.

14
00:00:56,574 --> 00:01:00,969
One: a Copilot Premium license with Agent Builder activated.

15
00:01:01,069 --> 00:01:05,143
Two: access to the project’s SharePoint site and Teams channels.

16
00:01:05,163 --> 00:01:07,921
The agent can only see what you can see.

17
00:01:08,021 --> 00:01:11,486
Three: transcription switched on for your project meetings,

18
00:01:11,506 --> 00:01:14,009
so the agent can read what was decided.

19
00:01:14,109 --> 00:01:16,605
And four: agreement on data rules.

20
00:01:16,625 --> 00:01:20,969
Project content only, and no personal or HR information.

21
00:01:21,969 --> 00:01:22,753
Step one.

22
00:01:22,773 --> 00:01:28,866
Open Microsoft 365 Copilot, go to Agents, and select Create agent.

23
00:01:29,366 --> 00:01:29,954
Step two.

24
00:01:29,974 --> 00:01:31,304
Agent Builder opens.

25
00:01:31,324 --> 00:01:37,264
You can describe the agent in plain words, but for full control, switch to Configure.

26
00:01:37,364 --> 00:01:42,629
Give it a clear name, such as Project Pulse, and a one-line description of what it does.

27
00:01:43,129 --> 00:01:44,894
Step three: the instructions.

28
00:01:44,914 --> 00:01:46,802
This is the heart of the agent.

29
00:01:46,822 --> 00:01:51,453
Tell it who it works for, what to produce, and the rules it must follow.

30
00:01:51,553 --> 00:01:54,822
Ask for a weekly status with a proposed rating,

31
00:01:54,842 --> 00:01:58,740
milestones, top risks, decisions, actions and open asks.

32
00:01:58,760 --> 00:02:00,980
Require a source for every line.

33
00:02:01,000 --> 00:02:05,958
And make it flag conflicts and gaps, instead of smoothing them over.

34
00:02:06,058 --> 00:02:10,148
Finally, list the risk signals to watch for: a date that slips,

35
00:02:10,168 --> 00:02:16,108
a dependency that is overdue, or a reassuring “should be fine” about something critical.

36
00:02:16,608 --> 00:02:17,996
Step four: knowledge.

37
00:02:18,016 --> 00:02:23,361
Add the project’s SharePoint site and key files, like the plan and the RAID log.

38
00:02:23,381 --> 00:02:27,470
Then switch on email, Teams chats and meetings as sources.

39
00:02:27,570 --> 00:02:31,482
Turn web search off, so answers come only from your project.

40
00:02:31,982 --> 00:02:32,588
Step five.

41
00:02:32,608 --> 00:02:38,349
Add starter prompts, so anyone can run the routine with one click: draft this week’s status,

42
00:02:38,369 --> 00:02:43,954
show new risks since Monday, and list decisions and actions from this week’s meetings.

43
00:02:44,454 --> 00:02:45,649
Step six: test it.

44
00:02:45,669 --> 00:02:50,240
Run the weekly status prompt in the preview, and check three things.

45
00:02:50,260 --> 00:02:51,725
Is every line sourced?

46
00:02:51,745 --> 00:02:53,210
Are conflicts flagged?

47
00:02:53,230 --> 00:02:55,725
Is anything confidential left out?

48
00:02:55,825 --> 00:03:00,177
When a test fails, add one rule to the instructions and run it again.

49
00:03:00,677 --> 00:03:02,527
Step seven: make it proactive.

50
00:03:02,547 --> 00:03:05,770
Schedule the status prompt for every Friday morning,

51
00:03:05,790 --> 00:03:10,541
and a short risk check every weekday, so the results are waiting for you.

52
00:03:10,641 --> 00:03:13,696
For instant alerts the moment a new risk appears,

53
00:03:13,716 --> 00:03:18,183
your Copilot Studio team can add an event trigger to the same agent.

54
00:03:18,683 --> 00:03:19,392
Step eight.

55
00:03:19,412 --> 00:03:24,955
Select Create, then share the agent with your project team, or keep it for yourself.

56
00:03:24,975 --> 00:03:29,613
Each person only ever sees the content they already have access to.

57
00:03:30,613 --> 00:03:32,549
Here is what that looks like.

58
00:03:32,569 --> 00:03:36,326
On Tuesday morning, an alert: the load board has slipped

59
00:03:36,346 --> 00:03:40,036
from week 48 to week 50, according to a supplier email.

60
00:03:40,056 --> 00:03:42,279
It is not in the risk log yet.

61
00:03:42,379 --> 00:03:47,795
The alert names the source, suggests an owner, and proposes an update to the risk log.

62
00:03:47,815 --> 00:03:49,848
You decide what happens next.

63
00:03:50,348 --> 00:03:55,602
On Friday, the status draft is ready: sourced, structured, with conflicts flagged.

64
00:03:55,622 --> 00:03:59,010
You review it in fifteen minutes instead of compiling

65
00:03:59,030 --> 00:04:02,124
it for three hours, set the rating, and send.

66
00:04:03,124 --> 00:04:04,546
Keep five guardrails.

67
00:04:04,566 --> 00:04:07,019
The agent respects your permissions.

68
00:04:07,039 --> 00:04:08,942
Every line names its source.

69
00:04:08,962 --> 00:04:12,446
The project manager owns every rating and decision.

70
00:04:12,466 --> 00:04:15,056
No personal data goes into the output.

71
00:04:15,076 --> 00:04:18,298
And a person checks before anything is sent.

72
00:04:19,098 --> 00:04:20,347
The agent gathers.

73
00:04:20,367 --> 00:04:21,343
You decide.

74
00:04:22,143 --> 00:04:27,554
Build your PM Agent this week, and give your Fridays back to the work that matters.
